-- let_forward_reference at 9:13, in its `self` reading (`language.md` §7): a
-- value binding is in scope inside its own right-hand side, but it has no
-- value there, so `x = x + 1` reads its own `const` in the temporal dead
-- zone. Only a FUNCTION can be recursive, which is why `countDown` — written
-- the same way one line down — is legal.
h =
    x = x + 1

    countDown k =
        if k == 0 then
            0
        else
            countDown (k - 1)
    x + countDown 3
